{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-driver","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"New Bash phase driver centralizes failure-sensitive Step 2b behavior and needs specialist review of shell semantics.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new design-postplan-emit.sh phase driver for Bash 3.2 compatibility, set -e safety, child command status capture, KV parsing, and mandatory result flushing on every success and operation-failure path. Check whether default statuses remain populated after EMIT, snapshot, validator, and usage/config branches, especially when helpers exit non-zero or omit expected keys. Verify that defects-found, skipped-quick, missing-diff-lines, and validator infrastructure failures map to the intended exit codes and statuses. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"handoff-kv","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change depends on consistent driver-to-orchestrator KV handoff across multiple markdown call sites.","prompt_body":"Inspect the Step 2b, Gate A, Gate B, and discussion-round2 call sites for consistent invocation of design-postplan-emit.sh and consistent parsing of .design-postplan-emit-result.env before stdout fallback. Pay close attention to symlink refusal, allowlisted keys, file-first precedence, stdout fill-only semantics, warning replay, mandatory-key aborts, and exit-code routing. Compare the call-site behavior against the driver contract so stale values or missing parse failures cannot route to the wrong repair, validator, or continuation path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"pause-flow","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The refactor collapses multiple pause checkpoints into a driver and could silently alter pause/resume control flow.","prompt_body":"Review cooperative pause preservation across the orchestrator prelude and the new driver-internal checkpoints. Verify that pause requests before EMIT, before snapshot, and before validator resolve ISSUE_NUMBER correctly from sourced environment or export-format source-env.sh and exec the pause-save script without running later steps. Check that non-pause paths still preserve plugin-root and design-tmpdir resolution without relying on ambient shell state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"doc-pin-drift","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"This diff migrates normative workflow prose and structural pins, where stale references can make future reviews vacuous.","prompt_body":"Check the documentation, skill prose, and structural-test pin migrations for drift after replacing inline EMIT, snapshot, and validator fences with design-postplan-emit.sh. Verify that flags.md, SKILL.md, approval-gates.md, discussion-rounds.md, design-postplan-emit.md, and scripts/test-design-structure.sh agree on quick validation, --force-validate, snapshot suppression, defects-found routing, and Step 2b.5 ordering. Look for vacuous greps or stale ACTION=EMIT_PLAN and invoke-plan-validator.sh prose that could cause double emits or fail to guard the new contract. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
